researchers will have the network build itself. "Cellular automata"
each one its one computer, will actually forge linkages.

De Garis calls this approach 'evolutionary engineering'. The neural
net grows when cellular automata send 'growth signals' to each other,
then connect via 'synapses'. Currently, the brain's logical innards are forming in two dimensions, though they will soon begin to interconnect in three
